# Wipe logs after every ship (Builder)

After **every** version bump + ship (MOD_VERSION / modinfo.ini / FLUFFY_INSTALL.txt updated):

1. Run `_wipe_game_logs.ps1` with the new version:
   ```powershell
   powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "_wipe_game_logs.ps1" -Version 3.0.XX
   ```
2. **Truncate only** — never `Remove-Item` / `os.remove` these files.

## Paths (always all three)

| Log | Path |
|-----|------|
| Quest Tracker | `C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Dragons Dogma 2\reframework\data\quest_tracker_log.txt` |
| REFramework | `C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Dragons Dogma 2\re2_framework_log.txt` |
| Fluffy MM | `C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Dragons Dogma 2\MM\Data\Log.txt` |

## Why

Coordinator + Audit read disk after user plays. Old lines from prior builds confuse version checks and cache errors.

## In-game (already handled)

`quest_tracker.lua` truncates `quest_tracker_log.txt` when MOD_VERSION in the file header differs from loaded version. Builder still wipes all three on ship so **re2** and **Fluffy** logs are clean before the user launches.

## Ship checklist tail

1. Bump version + implement fixes
2. **Run `_wipe_game_logs.ps1`**
3. Tell user: **INSTALL NEW MOD IN FLUFFY** then play, quit, **Audit if fail**
